#3. Metavelvet DL

#ASSEMBLY MODULE:  proving exceptionally hard to install and use.. removing from analysis, too time consuming) 

1. Construct a de Bruijn graph using Velvet functions.

   ~$ velveth Assem 31 -shortPaired -fastq rockfish_genus.R1.fastq.gz  rockfish_genus.R2.fastq.gz

   ~$ velvetg Assem -ins_length 500 -read_trkg yes -exp_cov auto

2. Extract candidates of chimeric nodes.
   ~$ metavelvete Assem -ins_length 500

3. Extract features from candidates of chimeric nodes.
   Extract Features

      ~$ perl FeatureExtractPredict.perl [out-dir]/meta-velvetg.subgraph__TitleChimeraNodeCandidates \
      [out-dir]/Features [out-dir]/Features3Class [out-dir]/ChimeraNodeName

4. Do classification using a trained deep learning model

   ~$ python metavelvet_dl_inference.py [data_directory] [model_path] [output_path]

5. Do assembly
   ~$ metavelvetg [out-dir] -ins_length [insert-length]#




